{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Reproach</b> — their reproach, with which they reproach me, has humbled my heart." "<b>And I am sick</b> — the alef is a sign of the speaker [first person]. Were the alef absent, it would be יאנש, and a shureq comes in place of a cholam, like ישפוטו הם." "<b>To mourn</b> — like 'to mourn for him.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 69, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:46.369138752Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}